layer norm is baically each row normalize with mean and variance and with a learned para gamma and beta, 
self attention block is basically when we try to 


h.0
│
├── ln_1
├── attn
│   ├── c_attn
│   └── c_proj
│
├── ln_2
└── mlp
    ├── c_fc
    └── c_proj

ln_1 — first LayerNorm

You'll have:

transformer.h.0.ln_1.weight
transformer.h.0.ln_1.bias

Both are:

wte = [50257, 768]
wpe = [1024, 768]

These are your LayerNorm:

γ = weight
β = bias

So:

normalized = (x - mean) / sqrt(variance + epsilon)

output = normalized * weight + bias
